Velero Installation


Helm =======>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>


Official Doc: https://helm.sh/docs/intro/install/


Helm CLI Installation Linux:

curl -fsSL -o get_helm.sh https://raw.githubusercontent.com/helm/helm/main/scripts/get-helm-3
chmod 700 get_helm.sh
./get_helm.sh
helm version



Helm CLI Installation Windows:

https://github.com/helm/helm/releases/tag/v3.17.1
vi .bashrc
export PATH=$PATH:/c/Program\ Files/helm/
source ~/.bashrc
helm version


Velero =======>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>


Official Doc: https://artifacthub.io/packages/helm/vmware-tanzu/velero


Velero CLI Installation Linux:

curl -LO https://github.com/vmware-tanzu/velero/releases/download/v1.15.2/velero-v1.15.2-linux-amd64.tar.gz
tar -xvf velero-v1.15.2-linux-amd64.tar.gz
sudo mv velero-v1.15.2-linux-amd64/velero /usr/local/bin/
rm -rf velero-v1.15.2-linux-amd64 velero-v1.15.2-linux-amd64.tar.gz






Velero Helm Installation:

helm repo add vmware-tanzu https://vmware-tanzu.github.io/helm-charts => Add helm chart
helm repo update
Run Below Command To Install Velero Helm Chart In Kubernetes Cluster:

helm install velero vmware-tanzu/velero \

--namespace velero --create-namespace \

--set-file credentials.secretContents.cloud=/home/arjun/.aws/credentials \

--set configuration.backupStorageLocation[0].name=default \

--set configuration.backupStorageLocation[0].provider=aws \

--set configuration.backupStorageLocation[0].bucket=findx-velero-backup-s3 \

--set configuration.backupStorageLocation[0].prefix=backup \

--set configuration.backupStorageLocation[0].config.region=us-east-1 \

--set configuration.volumeSnapshotLocation[0].name=default \

--set configuration.volumeSnapshotLocation[0].provider=aws \

--set configuration.volumeSnapshotLocation[0].config.region=us-east-1 \

--set initContainers[0].name=velero-plugin-for-aws \

--set initContainers[0].image=velero/velero-plugin-for-aws:v1.8.2 \

--set initContainers[0].volumeMounts[0].mountPath=/target \

--set initContainers[0].volumeMounts[0].name=plugins


velero backup-location get => Check if attached location is available.
kubectl get pods -n velero => List Running Pods.
To Backup Cluster Run Below COmmand:

velero backup create minikube-cluster-backup \
--exclude-namespaces kube-node-lease,kube-public,kube-system,velero \
--exclude-resources daemonsets \
--storage-location default


velero backup get => List Backups
velero restore create --from-backup minikube-cluster-backup => Restore Backups
velero schedule create daily-backup --schedule="0 */12 * * *" => Scheduled Backups
velero restore get => List Restored Backups
velero backup delete minikube-cluster-backup => Delete Backups
kubectl logs deployment/velero -n velero => Check Logs
helm uninstall velero -n velero => Uninstall Velero


